You can run it locally and see how much memory the R process consumes.
If you reduce the amount of data loaded such that it doesn't run out of memory on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>, we provide metrics at 1 minute granularity that can be viewed on the dashboard or obtained via the rsconnect package.
You can add gc() statements to your application to log memory usage.

I am sure there might be other ways, but honestly, I am not actually an expert at R. :)

